    </div>
    <div class="rec-data">Data: {esc(worst_cat['top_category'])} avg rating = {worst_cat['avg_rating']}; {int(poor_rating_products.shape[0])} products catalog-wide rated below 3.0</div>
  </div>

  <div class="rec-card">
    <div class="rec-title">3. Leverage Low-Discount, High-Rating Products as Trust Anchors</div>
    <div class="rec-body">
      {len(low_discount_high_rating)} products maintain ratings ≥4.2 with discounts ≤20%. These are your trust signals — products so good they don't need deep cuts. Feature them prominently in category landing pages and "top rated" merchandising slots. Their organic satisfaction will pull conversion more efficiently than promotional discounts.
    </div>
    <div class="rec-data">Data: {len(low_discount_high_rating)} products with discount ≤20% and rating ≥4.2; discount-rating correlation confirms discounts don't drive ratings</div>
  </div>

  <div class="rec-card">
    <div class="rec-title">4. Address Durability Concerns in High-Volume Low-Price Segments</div>
    <div class="rec-body">
